.TH CRDIR 1 "16 September 2026" "Andromeda" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
crdir \- create directories with a chosen owner, group, and mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crdir
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR owner ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR group ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR mode ]
.I dir
.RI [ dir " ...]"
.PP
.B crdir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crdir
creates one or more directories and then sets owner, group, and
permissions
.I only on the paths you named
.
Missing parent directories are created with
.BR mkdir (1)
.BR \-p
so the command works like
.B mkdir \-p
plus
.BR chown / chmod
on the leaf.
.PP
Parents that had to be created are
.I not
re\-owned.
That avoids turning
.B /srv
or
.B /srv/platforms
into
.B deploy:www\-data
mode 0770 by accident.
.PP
The usual job on
.B Andromeda
and the VPS is making Backdrop trees that both
.B deploy
(Git, Bee, SSH) and
.B www\-data
(Apache, PHP) must write:
.IP \(bu 3
.BI files/ site
.IP \(bu 3
.BI files_private/ site
.IP \(bu 3
.BI config/ site /active
.PP
Those three need the setgid bit
.RB ( \-s )
so new files inherit group
.BR www\-data .
Git\-tracked
.B config/*/staging
is normally created
.I without
.BR \-s .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " owner"
Directory owner.
Default:
.BR deploy .
.TP
.BI \-g " group"
Directory group.
Default:
.BR www\-data .
.TP
.BI \-m " mode"
Octal mode, with or without a leading zero.
Default:
.BR 0770
(owner and group may read, write, and enter; others have no access).
.TP
.B \-s
Set the setgid bit on each
.I named
directory
.RB ( chmod " g+s)."
New files and subdirectories created inside then keep group
.IR group .
Use this on public files, private files, and active config.
Do not use it on every parent you did not mean to share.
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run.
Print the
.BR mkdir ,
.BR chown ,
and
.BR chmod
commands with a leading
.B +
and do not run them.
User and group existence are not checked in this mode so you can
preview on a laptop.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built\-in help and exit.
The help is written for a first\-time sysadmin: what the tool is for,
which flags to use, a dry\-run first step, and a copy\-paste example.
.B \-\-help
is accepted anywhere on the command line.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
If you pass
.I no
directory arguments,
.B crdir
asks:
.PP
.RS
user  [deploy]:
.br
group [www\-data]:
.br
mode  [0770]:
.br
paths (space\-separated):
.RE
.PP
Press Enter to keep a default.
Type every path on one line, separated by spaces.
Paths that contain spaces cannot be entered this way; pass them as
command\-line arguments instead (quoted).
.PP
If directories
.I are
given on the command line, there are no prompts.
Missing
.BR \-o / \-g / \-m
values use the defaults.
That is the form to use in scripts and in
.BR newfeature .
.SH HOW OWNERSHIP IS APPLIED
For each named
.IR dir :
.IP 1. 3
If
.I dir
exists and is not a directory,
.B crdir
exits with an error and changes nothing further.
.IP 2. 3
If
.I dir
does not exist,
.B mkdir \-p
creates it and any missing parents.
.IP 3. 3
.B chown
.IR owner : group
and
.B chmod
.I mode
run on
.I dir
only.
.IP 4. 3
If
.B \-s
was given,
.B chmod g+s
runs on
.I dir
only.
.PP
An existing named directory is brought into line (idempotent).
Contents inside it are not changed.
This is not a recursive repair tool.
.PP
When the operator is not root,
.BR mkdir ,
.BR chown ,
and
.BR chmod
are run with
.BR sudo (8).
The rest of the script is not.
Default owner stays
.B deploy
even if you ran
.B sudo crdir
(do not do that; run
.B crdir
as
.B deploy
and let it sudo the three commands).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every named path is a directory.
In dry\-run mode, the plan was printed.
.TP
.B 1
Bad mode, unknown user or group, empty path list, or a named path
exists and is not a directory.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Must contain
.BR mkdir ,
.BR chown ,
.BR chmod ,
.BR id ,
.BR getent ,
.BR ls ,
and (when not root)
.BR sudo .
.SH FILES
No configuration file.
Defaults are compiled in to match the default stack:
.BR deploy ,
.BR www\-data ,
.BR 0770 .
.SH EXAMPLES
A first\-time sysadmin on the devel host can copy these as written.
.SS Preview before touching the disk
.nf
crdir \-n \-s \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files_private/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/config/www/active
.fi
.PP
Read the lines that start with
.BR + .
If they look right, run the same command without
.BR \-n .
.SS Devel checkout on the devel host (setgid trees)
These directories are written by both PHP and deploy.
.nf
crdir \-s \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files/kl \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files_private/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files_private/kl \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/config/www/active \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/config/kl/active
.fi
.SS Staging config (no setgid)
These directories are Git\-tracked and should stay deploy\-written.
.nf
crdir \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/config/www/staging \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/config/kl/staging
.fi
.SS Same layout on the VPS
Change only the Git root.
Test:
.nf
crdir \-s \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/files/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/files/kl \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/files_private/www \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/files_private/kl \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/config/www/active \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/config/kl/active

crdir \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/config/www/staging \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite\-test/config/kl/staging
.fi
.PP
Live: replace
.B ecom\-test
with
.BR ecom\-live .
.SS One directory, all flags spelled out
.nf
crdir \-o deploy \-g www\-data \-m 0770 \-s \e
  /srv/platforms/mysite/files/www
.fi
.SS Interactive (no arguments)
.nf
crdir
.fi
.PP
Accept the three defaults, then type the paths.
Useful at the local console when you do not want to remember flags.
.SS What a good result looks like
.nf
drwxrws--- 2 deploy www\-data 4096 Sep 16 18:00 files/thq
.fi
.PP
Letters:
.B rwx
for deploy,
.B rws
for www\-data (the
.B s
is setgid),
.B \-\-\-
for others.
User
.BR deploy ,
group
.BR www\-data .
.PP
Staging without
.B \-s
looks like
.B rwxrwx\-\-\-
(no
.B s
in the group column).
.SH WHY SETGID
Without
.BR \-s ,
the next file PHP writes is owned
.B www\-data:www\-data
and deploy cannot delete or commit it unless you add extra sudo.
With
.BR \-s ,
the file is
.B www\-data:www\-data
still as
.I user
but the
.I group
stays
.B www\-data
on the directory, and 0770 lets deploy in via the group.
.PP
Setgid does not change files that already exist inside the tree.
To repair an old tree you still need a separate
.B chown \-R
pass; that is out of scope for
.BR crdir .
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 3
Install the script on
.B PATH
as
.B crdir
(for example
.BR /usr/local/sbin/crdir )
and this page as
.BR /usr/local/share/man/man1/crdir.1 .
Then
.B man crdir
works.
Until then:
.B man ./crdir.1
from the directory that holds the page.
.IP \(bu 3
Do not run
.B sudo crdir
for the whole script.
Run it as
.BR deploy .
It will ask for a sudo password only for
.BR mkdir / chown / chmod .
.IP \(bu 3
.B crdir
never recursively changes files already in the directory.
.IP \(bu 3
Octal modes only.
.B u=rwx,g=rwx,o=
is rejected; write
.B 0770
instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR chown (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR install (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR ls (1)
